Cultured Code has <a href="https://culturedcode.com/things/support/articles/2409121/">updated</a> its task management app Things with support for the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a>, introducing an adaptive layout, a sidebar, and multi-window support ahead of the device's launch on Friday.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/things-3-for-iphone-duo.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072080" /><br/>
The app's interface adjusts to the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj;'s different configurations, including when it is closed, fully open, or partially folded like a book. The layout also supports both portrait and landscape orientations.<br/>
<br/>
Opening the device reveals a sidebar for switching between lists, which is a first for Things on the iPhone. Users can also open two Things windows side by side and drag and drop items between them to organize their tasks.<br/>
<br/>
Controls sit in a vertical bar within reach of the user's thumb. This includes Things' Magic Plus button, which can be dragged to a specific position in a list to insert a new to-do there.<br/>
<br/>
Connecting a keyboard enables the full set of Things' keyboard features, including a persistent selection, keyboard shortcuts, and Type Travel for quickly navigating between lists.<br/>
<br/>
